V3.0
-----
Play vs Coach King + Practice mode. New /play page: full interactive chess
game against a Claude-powered opponent with 4 difficulty levels and 4
coaching assistance levels. After each player mistake Coach King slides up
a panel explaining the error, showing the move sequence on a mini board
with prev/next navigation and "your move vs better move" tabs.
New /practice page: Claude-generated tactics puzzles (SAN answer checker,
per-puzzle mini board) and opening trainer (server-pre-computed FEN
sequences, board viewer with step navigation). Navigation bar links all
three pages. chess.css handles board rendering, highlights, and slide-up
mistake panel animation across the whole site.

V2.0
-----
Custom web UI with live agent visualization. FastAPI + WebSocket backend
serves a dark chess-themed frontend. Three agent nodes light up as they
become active. Arrows animate when data flows between nodes. Debug window
shows plain-English status in real time. Coach King's interview moves into
the browser with Web Speech API voice. CLI mode (main.py) still works.

V1.0
-----
Initial release. Core three-agent pipeline (Analyst → Coach → Critic).
Features: Chess.com integration, SQLite user memory, PGN parsing with
time-pressure detection, personalized coaching reports, PDF output,
Coach King character with macOS voice.
